      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "VIENNA CALLING (5) has been very consistent of late without winning. Those runs did come in tougher events than this in town. The seven week freshen up could well work in her favour coming back 300m in ground. The claim won't hurt either. HELL'S CITI (2) was very sound last preparation. He put himself onto the speed each time and battled hard. Can build on that now. EIGHTY MILE BEACH (3) has been a long time away from the track but had a good grounding for this return. Gets numerous gear changes for this. GUARD THE MULLAH (1) could also be up with the leaders. Did win first up at the last campaign. GOD'S WRATH (4) was never far away at most of his recent outings. Will need some luck off the draw.",
